{"operations":[{"content":"\"\"\"paths: URL path normalization.\"\"\"\n\n\ndef normalize(path):\n    \"\"\"Collapse repeated slashes and drop a trailing slash (except for the root).\"\"\"\n    if not path.startswith(\"/\"):\n        path = \"/\" + path\n    # Collapse multiple slashes\n    while \"//\" in path:\n        path = path.replace(\"//\", \"/\")\n    # Remove trailing slash if not root\n    if len(path) > 1 and path.endswith(\"/\"):\n        path = path[:-1]\n    return path\n","expected_sha256":"61f171916ec69e84b3e4873cc4eedb7c74682389a16b5654d791a31cc698a7d7","kind":"modify","path":"src/paths.py"}],"rationale":"The original normalize function only collapsed repeated slashes but did not remove a trailing slash (except for root). The fix adds a check to remove a trailing slash if the path is longer than one character, ensuring paths like '/users/me/' normalize to '/users/me', satisfying the defect requirement while keeping the existing API and tests intact."}